(
    version: 1,
    id: "m09",
    title: "Line Follower II",
    chapter: 3,
    concepts: ["PID tuning"],
    world: (id: "line_track", variant: Some("b")),
    robot: Starter("rover"),
    time_limit_s: 40.0,
    grading_seeds: [1, 2, 3],
    battery_soc: (0.7, 1.0),
    brief_md: r#"
## A faster lap with corners

This track has a long straight, a curve and **sharp corners**. Complete **one lap in 35 seconds or
less**, staying **within 25 mm** of the line.

A P controller reacts to where the robot is. A **D term** reacts to how fast the error is changing
and calms the wobble; an **I term** removes a steady offset. Tuning means finding gains that give a
fast lap without losing the line. Change one gain at a time and use `axl_plot` to watch the error.
"#,
    predict: Some((
        question: "The track is one closed loop. If the Rover drove it at a steady 0.15 m/s, how many seconds would one lap take?",
        unit: "s",
        measured: "lap_time_at_015_s",
    )),
    criteria: [FollowLine(max_dev_m: 0.025, laps: 1, within_s: 35.0)],
    stars: (
        (text: "A lap in under 20 seconds", criteria: [FollowLine(max_dev_m: 0.025, laps: 1, within_s: 20.0)]),
        (text: "Never more than 12 mm from the line", criteria: [FollowLine(max_dev_m: 0.012, laps: 1, within_s: 20.0)]),
    ),
    hints: (
        "Take your m08 follower and make the base speed depend on the error: slow down in corners, speed up on straights.",
        "derivative = error - previous_error. correction = kp * error + kd * derivative. Raise kd until the wobble on the straight disappears.",
        "Tune in this order: kp until it follows the curve, kd until it is calm, then raise the base speed and repeat. Add a little ki only if the Rover always sits on one side of the line.",
    ),
)
